# Column headers
crime-column-offense = Offense
crime-column-desc = Description
crime-column-notes = Notes
crime-column-code = Code


# Severity and sentencing
crime-severity-minor-name = Minor Crimes
crime-severity-minor-sentence = Maximum sentence for a minor crime is 5 minutes. Warnings should be issued for a first offense.
crime-severity-minor-code = 1-XX

crime-severity-moderate-name = Moderate Crimes
crime-severity-moderate-sentence = Maximum sentence is 5 minutes. A warning may be appropriate depending on the situation.
crime-severity-moderate-code = 2-XX

crime-severity-major-name = Major Crimes
crime-severity-major-sentence = Maximum sentence is 10 minutes. Reccomend avoiding maximum sentences for compliant individuals.
crime-severity-major-code = 3-XX

crime-severity-extreme-name = Extreme Crimes
crime-severity-extreme-sentence = Maximum sentence is 15 minutes.
crime-severity-extreme-code = 4-XX

crime-severity-capital-name = Capital Crimes
crime-severity-capital-sentence = Should usually lead to a death sentence or shift-lasting detainment.
crime-severity-capital-code = 5-XX

# Minor Crimes

crime-petty-theft-name = Petty Theft (H)
crime-petty-theft-desc = To take non-vital or inexpensive property of another individual, organization, or common property, without consent.
crime-petty-theft-notes = Petty theft covers the owning or possession of items that were not lawfully or consentually given to the holder. This may include departmental contraband if the contraband was not approved for the holder. Items covered by petty theft are usually easily replaceable, low-value, or low-danger.
crime-petty-theft-code = 1-01

crime-vandalism-name = Vandalism (D)
crime-vandalism-desc = To intentionally deface or superficially damage public or private property.
crime-vandalism-notes = Painting obscene graffiti, smashing bar glasses, breaking lights, and eating a crewmember's plushie is vandalism; breaking a window into space or secure areas is not.
crime-vandalism-code = 1-02

crime-trespass-name = Trespass (T)
crime-trespass-desc = To enter a non-secured area without permission.
crime-trespass-notes = It's best to just remove them from the area unless this is a repeated crime.
crime-trespass-code = 1-03

crime-animal-cruelty-name = Animal Cruelty (V)
crime-animal-cruelty-desc = To inflict unnecessary suffering or harm on a non-sapient being with malicious intent.
crime-animal-cruelty-notes = This doesn't include legitimate and authorized animal testing and usually doesn't extend to vermin such as mice, animals normally used in the process of food production, or creatures that could pose a threat to the station.
crime-animal-cruelty-code = 1-04

crime-endangerment-name = Endangerment (V)
crime-endangerment-desc = To recklessly put yourself or others in danger, either through direct action or failure to act.
crime-endangerment-notes = Covers industrial accidents, industrial negligence, self-experimentation, or even medical malpractice.
crime-endangerment-code = 1-05

crime-disturbance-name = Disturbance (R)
crime-disturbance-desc = To cause a public disturbance.
crime-disturbance-notes = Sometimes referred to as hooliganism. The catch-all for obnoxious crewmates. Covers things such as public nudity, needless insults, obstructing authorities, and inciting crime or violence.
crime-disturbance-code = 1-06

# Moderate Crimes

crime-resisting-search-name = Resisting a Lawful Search (E)
crime-resisting-search-desc = To resist a reasonable or lawful search or seizure by a member of the security department, or an authorized head of staff.
crime-resisting-search-notes = The search or seizure must be legal, either through a valid warrant, evidence, or alert level. The perpetrator must have made an active attempt to flee, resist restraint, or refuse to hand over contraband if applicable.
crime-resisting-search-code = 2-00

crime-grand-theft-name = Grand Theft (H)
crime-grand-theft-desc = To take critical or unreplaceable property of another individual or organization without consent.
crime-grand-theft-notes = The difference between theft and grand theft is based on how crucial the stolen item is. This is mostly used for the theft of command staff items such as door remotes, hardsuits, jetpacks, and unreplaceable machine parts. Additionally, stealing anything from the armory is grand theft, including seized contraband.
crime-grand-theft-code = 2-01

crime-damage-property-name = Damage of Property (D)
crime-damage-property-desc = To maliciously damage or deface public or private property or equipment.
crime-damage-property-notes = Includes destruction of job equipment, such as hydro trays, booze dispensers, and chemical dispensers. A step up from vandalism but a step down from critical property destruction.
crime-damage-property-code = 2-02

crime-secure-trespass-name = Secure Trespass (T)
crime-secure-trespass-desc = To enter a secured area without permission.
crime-secure-trespass-notes = This covers places like telecomms, head offices, security zones, command areas, the vault, and the armory.
crime-secure-trespass-code = 2-03

crime-assault-name = Assault (V)
crime-assault-desc = To threaten to or to use physical force against a member of the crew without the intent to kill.
crime-assault-notes = Attempted murder and assault are different; a fist fight is most likely assault, while a shooting may be an attempted murder. Ensure you have context before making the call.
crime-assault-code = 2-04

crime-gross-negligence-name = Gross Negligence (V)
crime-gross-negligence-desc = A conscious, reckless disregard for the safety or wellbeing of others.
crime-gross-negligence-notes = To cause an unreasonable amount of damage to a part of the station as a result of negligence. This could be purposefully allowing anomalies to go critical, or causing an accidental but not permanent death.
crime-gross-negligence-code = 2-05

# Major Crimes

crime-obstruction-justice-name = Obstruction of Justice (E)
crime-obstruction-justice-desc = To intentionally impede or otherwise prevent a member of the security department from enforcing the law.
crime-obstruction-justice-notes = This applies to attempting to prevent an officer from making a lawful arrest, detainment, or execution.
crime-obstruction-justice-code = 3-00

crime-minor-sabotage-name = Minor Sabotage/Destruction (D)
crime-minor-sabotage-desc = To cause minor damage to an area or a minor station system.
crime-minor-sabotage-notes = Includes destruction of station machinery such as ID card computers or telecommunications servers, power devices such as substations, and non-hostile silicon units.
crime-minor-sabotage-code = 3-02

crime-kidnapping-name = Kidnapping (V)
crime-kidnapping-desc = To unlawfully restrain, transport, control, or confine a sapient being against that individual's will.
crime-kidnapping-notes = A large range of things, used mostly as a catch-all when dealing with unlawful control of another being.
crime-kidnapping-code = 3-04

crime-rioting-name = Rioting (R)
crime-rioting-desc = To take part in a large group of personnel creating an unlawful public disturbance.
crime-rioting-notes = Leaders of a riot can be charged with all crimes that happen under their lead.
crime-rioting-code = 3-06

# Extreme Crimes

crime-breach-custody-name = Breach of Custody (E)
crime-breach-custody-desc = To break out of a cell or custody with the intention of escaping.
crime-breach-custody-notes = Includes breaking out other people.
crime-breach-custody-code = 4-00

crime-major-sabotage-name = Major Sabotage/Destruction (D)
crime-major-sabotage-desc = To cause massive damage to an area or major station system.
crime-major-sabotage-notes = This is mostly used for deadly departmental bombings or sabotage of major station systems such as the TEG or hacking the ATS.
crime-major-sabotage-code = 4-02

crime-attempted-murder-name = Attempted Murder (V)
crime-attempted-murder-desc = To try to use force against a crewmember with the clear intent to kill.
crime-attempted-murder-notes = This covers any intentional but unsuccessful attempt to kill another member of the crew.
crime-attempted-murder-code = 4-04

crime-manslaughter-name = Manslaughter (V)
crime-manslaughter-desc = To incidentally kill a crewmember without intent.
crime-manslaughter-notes = Includes manslaughter in self-defense and negligent manslaughter. If there is provable intent, then the subject should instead be charged with attempted murder.
crime-manslaughter-code = 4-05

# Capital Crimes

crime-breach-permanent-confinement-name = Breach of Permanent Confinement (E)
crime-breach-permanent-confinement-desc = To break someone sentenced to Permanent Confinement out of a cell or custody with the intention of escaping.
crime-breach-permanent-confinement-notes = Includes breaking out other people sentenced to Permanent Confinement.
crime-breach-permanent-confinement-code = 5-00

crime-station-destruction-name = Station-Wide Destruction (D)
crime-station-destruction-desc = To engage in maliciously destructive actions which threaten to destroy, or successfully destroy a vessel or habitat.
crime-station-destruction-notes = Summed up, extreme sabotage of station systems or setting off self-destruction systems. This includes any means causing the entire station to become uninhabitable, releasing an active singularity, station-wide atmospherics sabotage, and destruction of the station AI.
crime-station-destruction-code = 5-02

crime-murder-name = Murder (V)
crime-murder-desc = To permanently kill a member of the crew.
crime-murder-notes = This covers any successful attempt to kill a member of the crew and prevent resuscitation. If the victim was declared legally dead but was able to be resuscitated, then it is only Attempted Murder.
crime-murder-code = 5-04

crime-mass-violence-name = Mass Acts of Violence (V)
crime-mass-violence-desc = To attempt to kill three or more sapient beings with malicious intent.
crime-mass-violence-notes = Applies when there have been three or more Attempted Murders with the intention to kill, or if the perpetrator has committed three or more acts of Manslaughter.
crime-mass-violence-code = 5-05

crime-mental-shielding-name = Refusal of Mental Shielding (R)
crime-mental-shielding-desc = To refuse to comply with a reasonable Mind Shielding procedure.
crime-mental-shielding-notes = Applies if the suspect is excessively uncooperative or the implant fails to function due to the mental state of the prisoner already being too far gone. If the implant fails, execution is heavily recommended.
crime-mental-shielding-code = 5-06
